§ `SCA-RTS Chapter II — Security measures for the application of SCA`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Chapter II, Articles 4 to 9.
-- OJ L 69, 13.3.2018, p. 28.
--
-- Articles 4 and 5 carry countable rules and are encoded: the authentication
-- code, the five-attempt block, the five-minute inactivity timeout, and
-- dynamic linking including the two travel-shaped variants in Art 5(3) --
-- consent to a blocked amount, and a consented batch to several payees.
--
-- Articles 6 to 9 are DELIBERATELY NOT ENCODED beyond Art 4(1)'s countable
-- "two or more elements". A requirement that measures be "adopted" to
-- "mitigate the risk" that an element is "uncovered by unauthorised parties"
-- is not a proposition an engine can evaluate, and is not faked into one
-- here. NOTES.md section 2 records the boundary.
--
-- Source text: registers/source-bundle/reg-del-2018-389.txt
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Article 4 — Authentication code`

-- Art 4(1): two or more elements from distinct categories.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 4(1)"
`minimum number of authentication element categories` MEANS 2

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 4(1)"
GIVEN `categories used` IS A LIST OF `Authentication Element Category`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authentication is based on enough distinct categories` IF
    count `categories used` AT LEAST `minimum number of authentication element categories`

-- Art 4(3)(b): consecutive failed attempts before the action is blocked
-- "shall not exceed five within a given period of time".
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 4(3)(b)"
`maximum consecutive failed authentication attempts` MEANS 5

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 4(3)(b)"
GIVEN `consecutive failed attempts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action must be blocked` IF
    `consecutive failed attempts` AT LEAST `maximum consecutive failed authentication attempts`

-- Art 4(3)(d): inactivity timeout for online payment account access.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 4(3)(d)"
`maximum minutes without payer activity after authentication` MEANS 5

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 4(3)(d)"
GIVEN `minutes without activity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authenticated session has timed out` IF
    `minutes without activity` GREATER THAN `maximum minutes without payer activity after authentication`


§§ `Article 5 — Dynamic linking`

-- Art 5(1): where SCA applies under Art 97(2) PSD2 — remote electronic
-- payment transactions — the code must be dynamically linked to amount and
-- payee, and any change to either invalidates it.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 5(1)"
GIVEN `payer is made aware of the amount and the payee`             IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the code is specific to the amount and the payee`            IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the accepted code corresponds to the original amount and payee identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `any change to the amount or the payee invalidates the code`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dynamic linking requirements are met` IF
        `payer is made aware of the amount and the payee`
    AND `the code is specific to the amount and the payee`
    AND `the accepted code corresponds to the original amount and payee identity`
    AND `any change to the amount or the payee invalidates the code`

-- Art 5(3)(a): where the payer consented to an exact amount to be blocked
-- under Art 75(1) PSD2, the code is specific to THAT blocked amount. This is
-- the pre-authorisation case a hotel or a car-hire desk uses.
-- Art 5(3)(b): for a consented batch, the code is specific to the TOTAL of
-- the batch and to the specified payees. This is the multi-payee travel
-- basket case.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 5(3)"
GIVEN `is a card-based transaction with consent to an exact blocked amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `is a consented batch of remote electronic transactions`               IS A BOOLEAN
    , `blocked amount consented to`                                          IS A NUMBER
    , `total amount of the batch`                                            IS A NUMBER
    , `amount the code is specific to`                                       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authentication code is specific to the right amount` IF
    IF   `is a card-based transaction with consent to an exact blocked amount`
    THEN `amount the code is specific to` EQUALS `blocked amount consented to`
    ELSE IF   `is a consented batch of remote electronic transactions`
         THEN `amount the code is specific to` EQUALS `total amount of the batch`
         ELSE TRUE


-- ===========================================================================
-- CHAPTER III — EXEMPTIONS FROM STRONG CUSTOMER AUTHENTICATION
--
-- Every Article below states a POWER, not a duty: "payment service providers
-- shall be allowed not to apply strong customer authentication". Each
-- predicate therefore answers "is the exemption AVAILABLE", never "is SCA
-- disapplied" — the decision to take an available exemption stays with the
-- provider, and for a card transaction the issuer may decline an exemption
-- the acquirer requested. See NOTES.md §5.
-- ===========================================================================



